{"title":"The Mariner","logline":"In a post-collapse urban wasteland, a nautical-themed vigilante rescues his estranged sister from mobsters, only to face an existential crisis when she shatters the idealized memory of the father who inspired his heroic code.","synopsis":"Following a cascading societal collapse that turns urban downtowns into lawless ruins, Billy MacAngus operates as 'The Mariner,' a brutish vigilante clad in fisherman gear wielding a bloodied wooden oar. Tracking an AirTag he planted in his sister Rose's purse, he storms the mob-controlled Ruddy & Greene building, slaughtering thugs across multiple floors to extract her. However, Rose refuses to leave without her purse, revealing she intentionally robbed mob boss Mr. Salvatori of a blockchain ledger containing twenty million dollars.

As the siblings fight their way up to the luxurious 15th-floor penthouse to retrieve the purse, Billy proudly attributes his strength, resilience, and strict moral code to idyllic childhood lessons taught by his late father. Rose bluntly shatters this illusion, revealing their father never died heroically; he was an abusive, neglectful deadbeat on welfare who beat Billy and abandoned the family for another woman, while Billy sanitized the trauma into a myth of fatherly guidance.

Before Billy can process the truth, Salvatori and his enforcers ambushes them at gunpoint. Crushed and disoriented, Billy loses the will to fight and renounces his heroic persona. Facing execution, Rose gives a defiant speech reminding Billy that his courage and moral compass did not come from a deadbeat father, but from his own choice to rise above abuse. Reinvigorated by the truth of his self-made identity, The Mariner prepares to strike back.","act_structure":[{"act_number":1,"title":"Setup","start_scene":"EXT. CITY CENTRE - NIGHT","end_scene":"INT. RUDDY & GREEN BUILDING - ELEVATOR","summary":"The Mariner infiltrates a fortified skyscraper to rescue his sister Rose, fighting off goons and escaping into the elevator.","turning_points":["The Mariner uses an AirTag to track Rose to the mob-occupied Ruddy & Greene building.","The Mariner extracts Rose from captivity and takes the elevator down, believing the mission is a straightforward rescue."]},{"act_number":2,"title":"Confrontation","start_scene":"INT. RUDDY & GREEN BUILDING - ELEVATOR","end_scene":"INT. 15TH FLOOR","summary":"Rose reveals she stole twenty million dollars from mob boss Salvatori, forcing the duo to fight their way up to the penthouse to retrieve her purse containing the blockchain key.","turning_points":["Rose forces them to go up rather than escape so she can retrieve her crypto password.","Mariner subdues Rosco and learns Rose intentionally stole twenty million dollars of gang money.","Mariner eliminates Vinnie and his crew using a flare gun and brute force, reaching the 15th-floor office."]},{"act_number":3,"title":"Climax & Resolution","start_scene":"INT. 15TH FLOOR","end_scene":"INT. STAIRWELL / 15TH FLOOR OFFICE","summary":"Rose shatters Billy's romanticized memories of their father before Salvatori corners them, prompting Rose to redefine Billy's heroism so he can fight back.","turning_points":["Rose reveals their father is an alive deadbeat who neglected and beat Billy, triggering traumatic unvarnished flashbacks.","Salvatori ambushes the siblings, causing a demoralized Billy to disarm and surrender.","Rose re-frames Billy's heroism as a triumph of his own moral willpower over abuse, giving him the resolve to fight."]}],"themes":[{"theme":"The Myth vs. Reality of Idols","description":"The story deconstructs how individuals construct comforting mythologies around abusive or absent parents to cope with childhood trauma.","evidence":["Billy's initial golden-lit flashbacks of his father teaching him boxing and fishing.","Rose revealing their father is alive in Chimney Bay and was an abusive drunk who ditched Billy in a yard.","The stark revised flashbacks showing the father punching young Billy and calling him 'a bag a sad'."]},{"theme":"Self-Forged Heroism","description":"True virtue and moral courage are conscious individual choices rather than traits inherited from ancestry or external codes.","evidence":["Billy reciting the Mariner's code of 'honesty, bravery, and grit' derived from his father's words.","Rose stating: 'He somehow turned a deadbeat father into a superhero. Then became a real one.'"]},{"theme":"Sibling Protection and Loyalty","description":"Despite annoyance, ideological clashes, and deception, deep familial bonds drive mutual survival in an anarchic world.","evidence":["Billy planting an AirTag at Thanksgiving to keep tabs on Rose's safety.","Rose using her final confrontation with Salvatori not to plead for her life, but to rebuild her brother's shattered spirit."]}],"narrative_arc":"The narrative follows a classical siege-inversion arc paired with an internal psychological deconstruction: a vigilante completes a violent physical rescue, only to be dragged deeper into danger for material stakes, culminating in the destruction of his psychological origin story and his rebirth as a self-made hero.","genre":"Action / Vigilante Noir / Dark Comedy","tone":"Gritty, visceral, darkly comedic, and emotionally poignant.","protagonist_journey":"Billy begins as a naive, brutish vigilante operating under an inherited 'Mariner's code' built upon the romanticized memory of his father. When confronted with the reality of his childhood abuse and paternal abandonment, he collapses into despair, but is transformed into an authentically self-defined hero through his sister's recognition of his own innate goodness.","central_conflict":"Billy and Rose must survive the deadly enforcers of Mr. Salvatori's crime syndicate while navigating Billy's internal unraveling when his foundational life story is exposed as a lie.","setting_overview":"A near-future dystopian urban center, ruined and abandoned following the 2020 pandemic and a 2025 financial collapse, centered inside the dilapidated sandstone skyscraper of the Ruddy & Greene building.","confidence":0.98}
